  ('accommodation', 'noun', '/əˌkɒm.əˈdeɪ.ʃən/', 'Lodging in a dwelling or similar living quarters afforded to travellers in hotels or on cruise ships, or students, etc.', 'I have booked the accommodation for my trip to Paris.', 'wiktionary', 'B2', 'cefr-j'),
